# Apply-from marker for the migration runner
#
# The runner ONLY executes migration files whose filename sorts at or after
# this value. Anything older is skipped entirely and is never recorded in
# `schema_migrations`.
#
# Why this exists
# ---------------
# The migration files dated 2026_08_* predate the runner and were applied by
# hand, so there is no record of them in `schema_migrations`. Re-running them
# is not safe:
#
#   * 2026_08_12 and 2026_08_26 use a plain `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN`,
#     which fails with ER_DUP_FIELDNAME.
#   * 2026_08_22 adds a UNIQUE key on user_token that 2026_08_24 deliberately
#     drops again — re-running it would silently re-introduce the
#     single-session restriction that the multi-session migration removed.
#
# Rather than tracking that with a "baseline" list (which can be forgotten if
# the file is not deployed alongside), the runner simply refuses to look at
# anything before this marker. One rule, no exceptions, no chance of a
# conflict with the legacy migrations.
#
# Format: a single date prefix, matching the start of a migration filename.
# Everything from that prefix onwards is managed by the runner.

2026_10_22
